Add CLI description extraction.

The CLI can show a complete ticket and read individual metadata values, but it cannot extract the
ticket description without metadata or comments. Add a `description` command with this syntax:

    ticket description <id> [--short | --detailed]

With no selection option, the command should write the complete description, including the short
description and detailed description. `--short` should write only the first description line.
`--detailed` should write only description content after the first line. Metadata, description
separators, and comments must not be included in any output mode.

The selection options must be mutually exclusive. Output should preserve description text and line
breaks in the selected range, with one final newline for non-empty output. A missing detailed
description should produce empty output and a successful exit status. Existing ticket ID, file
read, and parse errors should use normal CLI error handling.


